---
import LetsTalk from '@components/home/LetsTalk.astro'
import Insight from '@components/insights/Insight.astro'
import InsightSignoff from '@components/insights/InsightSignoff.astro'
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
import { getInsightNav } from '@data/insights'
import InsightNav from '@components/insights/InsightNav.astro'

const { previous, current, next } = getInsightNav('when-should-you-rebuild-your-website')
---

<Layout title={current?.title} description={current?.summary}>
  <Insight tags={current?.tags}>
    <span slot="insight-title">{current?.title}</span>
    <span slot="insight-subtitle">{current?.dateLabel}</span>
    <span slot="insight-text">
      <p>
        Before committing to a website rebuild, it is worth asking why you think you need one. A rebuild is a
        significant investment, and the right answer is not always obvious. Sometimes the problem that feels like it
        needs a rebuild is actually something more targeted. And sometimes what looks manageable is actually overdue
        for replacement. Here is how to tell the difference.
      </p><br />
      <p><strong>Signs a rebuild is warranted:</strong></p>
      <ul class="lg:mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>The tech stack is deprecated or unsupported:</strong> If the platform or framework your site is built
            on no longer receives updates, you are accumulating risk. Security vulnerabilities, broken integrations, and
            incompatible plugins become increasingly expensive to manage the longer you leave it.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>The code is blocking business value:</strong> If making changes that should be simple requires significant
            developer effort, or the site actively prevents you from implementing things that would help the business,
            the underlying architecture is the problem.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>The UX and data flow are fundamentally wrong:</strong> Surface-level fixes cannot repair a site where
            the structure itself sends users in the wrong direction.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>Maintenance costs are compounding:</strong> When the annual cost of keeping the current site running
            is approaching or exceeding what a rebuild would cost, the economics have shifted.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <br />
      <p><strong>Signs a rebuild probably is not the answer:</strong></p>
      <ul class="lg:mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>The design feels dated but the structure works:</strong> A template refresh, updated imagery, or revised
            copy can make a significant difference without touching the underlying site.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>One integration is broken:</strong> A proper fix to a broken integration is not a reason to rebuild the
            entire site.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            <strong>You have not tested the actual problem:</strong> Low traffic or conversion rates are not automatically
            a website problem. Before attributing them to poor UX, check whether your SEO is working and whether the site
            has actually been tested with a meaningful volume of visitors.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <br />
      <p>
        Diagnosis matters here. A <a href="/services/discovery" class="underline underline-offset-2">discovery phase</a>
        or a <a href="/services/consulting" class="underline underline-offset-2">consulting conversation</a> is often the
        most cost-effective first step, it helps you make this call with evidence rather than instinct.
      </p><br />
      <InsightSignoff />
    </span>
  </Insight>

  <InsightNav previousInsight={previous} nextInsight={next} />

  <LetsTalk config={{ buttons: 'both', primaryCta: 'message' }} />
</Layout>
